# SHA-256 of every upstream file this package ships unmodified from box3d v0.1.0
# (tag v0.1.0, commit 8441b4a06d6d09dcfb0b0f704df4d847d1437b92,
# https://github.com/erincatto/box3d.git).
#
# 349 records. Box3D is a whole project rather than one vendored file, so this
# list is the complete regular-file inventory of the pinned upstream tree as it
# stands in this working copy: `src/`, `include/`, `test/`, `shared/`,
# `benchmark/`, `samples/`, `data/`, `docs/`, `extern/` and the top-level CMake
# project files all travel, including the parts this build compiles none of
# (samples, benchmarks, the Doxygen `docs/` tree and its images, the vendored
# sokol headers). The audit surface stays the whole upstream tree rather than a
# hand-picked subset of it.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   .gitignore -- upstream's fifteen lines are kept verbatim and this fork
#     appends its own ignore entries after them, so the file is no longer
#     byte-identical to upstream's. The pristine upstream digest is recorded as
#     a comment on its own line below rather than as a checkable record.
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, build_support/, zig/, runtime/, tests.zig,
#   smoke.zig, consumer/, cross-test.profile.sh,
#   .github/workflows/verify.yml, tools/, UPSTREAM.sha256, UPSTREAM.md,
#   NOTICE.md, README.md, README.zig.md, FORK-LICENSE.md, CHANGELOG.md,
#   FORK-NOTES.md, package.nix, flake.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml and .envrc
#     -- this fork's own files, listed in NOTICE.md. flake.lock and devenv.lock
#     are not in the tree either: they are the driver's to create, and this
#     record does not cover generated files.
#
# One record names a path that is not the upstream path. Upstream's README.md was
# preserved byte for byte as README.upstream.md when this fork's README.md took
# over the fork README, so the record reads README.upstream.md with the digest
# it always had: 2525d7ca5823027918c6ad7d84c1f9b946ef654d3350390e02a7dbe11aa5754e.
# The bytes are unchanged; only the name in the tree moved, and the name in a
# record has to move with the file.
#
# These are the bytes in this working tree, hashed on 2026-10-04 immediately
# after the archive import, with no Git command involved. They are not a
# signature and not a Git object id: UPSTREAM.md, "Integrity", states what they
# do and do not establish.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
# or, including the licence and README-presence checks:
#   tools/check-provenance.sh
#
# Pristine upstream `.gitignore`, 150 bytes, for the record only:
#   2295f05d5e1510d1d5e459c227cc35b046097eaaa8cd92c10c7ce51a9f9144ec  .gitignore
